n exists covering package metadata, pinned image references, and the validation manifest\n46\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be run through the validation harness against a target release, producing a deterministic pass/fail result\n47\t- The format supports both launch target types: workbench (notebook) tutorials and pipeline tutorials\n48\t- A tutorial's version and validation status can change without requiring a Dashboard release (packaging is independent of Dashboard release cadence)\n49\t\n50\t## HLR Traceability\n51\t\n52\t- HLR-3 (P1, primary): tutorial packaging format defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases\n53\t- Enables HLR-1 and HLR-2: the gallery and all curated tutorials are built against this format\n54\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-853b37eb0f858079","agent_id":"a98acb72dc71e745d","session_id":"0ad94842-2610-4147-8d08-4293ba16f19d","uuid":"f70edfa9-4931-44f2-a1d0-09d185c9b47a","timestamp":"2026-10-23T19:57:24.025Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-84a371e45c5bc7c3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
