not separately schedulable behind the P0 work because the same surface (metadata schema, pinned images, validation manifest) is what the gallery consumes and every tutorial is packaged with. Splitting would produce two epics building the same format. |\n55\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E005 | **docs-authoring priority exception:** the epic's priority is derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1, not from HLR-4's P2 label; docs epics do not push priority upstream. |\n56\t\n57\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n58\t\n59\t## Health Warnings\n60\t\n61\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no non-functional requirements. Teams were inferred from the architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). Open Questions section states \"None\" — no Investigation epics generated.\n62\t- **Component span on E001:** the packaging format covers both notebook and pipeline tutorials; the epic is assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks` (five of six tutorials are notebook-based, and pinned workbench images are the Notebooks domain per `notebooks.md`). Logged here as a non-obvious mapping.\n63\t- **Passive components:** Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines require no code changes for launch — the Dashboard already spawns workbenches and imports pipelines per `dashboard.md`. Their validation is an acceptance criterion on E002 (launch works end-to-end) and on E003/E004 (tutorials tested against the current release). No separate validation epics: the validating teams are the same teams that author the tutorials.\n64\t- **Tutorials touching components outside the affected list:** the first-deployment and first-RAG-app tutorials exercise serving components (KServe, Llama Stack) that are not in the strategy's Affected Components. They are consumed, not changed — no epics generated; noted as scope context on E003.\n65\t- **Effort / re-split trigger on E003:** authoring and release-testing five tutorials may exceed one sprint. Kept as ONE logical change because a split would fragment a single curated, consistently-styled tutorial set reviewed under one content process. **Re-split trigger:** split E003 by journey (e.g., workbench/data-prep vs training/deployment/RAG) if authoring plus validation exceeds a sprint of effort or if review throughput forces staggered delivery.\n66\t\n67\t## Tiered Delivery\n68\t\n69\tNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing — all work is in-platform against GA components, so no Tier 1/Tier 2 split is needed.\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b228d5d8c46820f5","agent_id":"a632e6c796703ddb2","session_id":"0ad94842-2610-4147-8d08-4293ba16f19d","uuid":"c895f280-305a-4903-82cd-71484c47e0dc","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:01:50.347Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab88ba684f70cf21","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
