{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a4b1a7b67af431f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019: Curated getting-started tutorial gallery\n11\t\n12\t## Epic List\n13\t\n14\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n15\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n16\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial packaging format and validation harness | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n17\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Dashboard tutorial gallery and one-click launch | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |\n18\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Author five notebook-based curated tutorials | Implementation | Workbenches | P0 |\n19\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Author the first-pipeline curated tutorial | Implementation | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 |\n20\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Document gallery usage and tutorial contribution process | Implementation | RHOAI Documentation | P1 |\n21\t\n22\t## Dependency DAG\n23\t\n24\t```mermaid\n25\tgraph TD\n26\t    E001[RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 Tutorial packaging format] --> E002[RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 Dashboard gallery]\n27\t    E001 --> E003[RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 Notebook tutorials]\n28\t    E001 --> E004[RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 Pipeline tutorial]\n29\t    E001 --> E005[RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 Documentation]\n30\t    E002 --> E005\n31\t    E003 --> E005\n32\t    E004 --> E005\n33\t```\n34\t\n35\t## DAG Justification\n36\t\n37\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n38\t|------|------|-----------|\n39\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The tutorial packaging format (metadata schema, pinned image references, validation manifest) is an artifact the Dashboard gallery code builds against — the gallery renders and launches packaged tutorials. Consuming Implementation is serial after the producing one. |\n40\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The five notebook tutorials are packaged (metadata, pinned images) and validated per the format; authoring testable tutorials requires the format and validation manifest to exist first. |\n41\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n42\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation is blocked by ALL Implementation epics in the strategy; the contribution process documents the packaging format itself. |\n43\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Gallery-usage documentation describes what was built. |\n44\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Docs describe the shipped tutorial set. |\n45\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Docs describe the shipped tutorial set. |\n46\t\n47\tNo konflux-onboarding, license-validation, or repo-onboarding epics are generated: all code components involved (Dashboard, Notebooks, Data Science Pipelines) exist in architecture context and are already Konflux-onboarded per their context files.\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n50\t\n51\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n52\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n53\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E002 | Dashboard gallery with one-click launch into the user's project. |\n54\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E003, E004 | Single HLR split by component/team boundary (Rule 1), not by priority: the five notebook-journey tutorials are Notebooks/Workbenches content; the first-pipeline tutorial is a Data Science Pipelines artifact authored and reviewed by the Pipelines team. Both halves are P0. |\n55\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 | **Bundled / priority-inheritance analysis:** the packaging-format epic is P0 by inheritance — it transitively enables all HLR-1 and HLR-2 work (the gallery and every tutorial build against the format), and an epic blocking all P0 work is implicitly P0. The P1 label on HLR-3 reads as relative value, not a deferral signal: the format is not separately schedulable behind the P0 work because the same surface (metadata schema, pinned images, validation manifest) is what the gallery consumes and every tutorial is packaged with. Splitting would produce two epics building the same format. |\n56\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E005 | **docs-authoring priority exception:** the epic's priority is derived from the strategy frontmatter `priority: Major` → P1, not from HLR-4's P2 label; docs epics do not push priority upstream. |\n57\t\n58\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n59\t\n60\t## Health Warnings\n61\t\n62\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no Dependencies table, no Given/When/Then acceptance criteria, and no non-functional requirements. Teams were inferred from the architecture-context owning teams (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard; Notebooks → Workbenches; Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). Open Questions section states \"None\" — no Investigation epics generated.\n63\t- **Component span on E001:** the packaging format covers both notebook and pipeline tutorials; the epic is assigned the single most-relevant canonical component `Notebooks` (five of six tutorials are notebook-based, and pinned workbench images are the Notebooks domain per `notebooks.md`). Logged here as a non-obvious mapping. Shared ownership of the format is made explicit by a cross-team review AC on E001: the RHOAI Pipelines team reviews and signs off the pipeline launch-target portion of the format specification.\n64\t- **Passive components:** Notebooks and Data Science Pipelines require no code changes for launch — the Dashboard already spawns workbenches and imports pipelines per `dashboard.md`. Their validation is an acceptance criterion on E002 (launch works end-to-end) and on E003/E004 (tutorials tested against the current release). No separate validation epics: the validating teams are the same teams that author the tutorials.\n65\t- **Tutorials touching components outside the affected list:** the first-deployment and first-RAG-app tutorials exercise serving components (KServe, Llama Stack) that are not in the strategy's Affected Components. They are consumed, not changed — no epics generated; noted as scope context on E003.\n66\t- **Effort / re-split trigger on E003:** authoring and release-testing five tutorials may exceed one sprint. Kept as ONE logical change because a split would fragment a single curated, consistently-styled tutorial set reviewed under one content process. **Re-split trigger:** split E003 by journey (e.g., workbench/data-prep vs training/deployment/RAG) if authoring plus validation exceeds a sprint of effort or if review throughput forces staggered delivery.\n67\t\n68\t## Tiered Delivery\n69\t\n70\tNot applicable. There are no external dependencies with uncertain timing — all work is in-platform against GA components, so no Tier 1/Tier 2 split is needed.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af63cdb71743c457","agent_id":"ad50c4934507a86db","session_id":"0ad94842-2610-4147-8d08-4293ba16f19d","uuid":"4fbaecc2-fa4a-49b4-be1c-2bc7a7a2a613","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:02:48.858Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9a4b1a7b67af431f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019"}
