n exists covering package metadata, pinned image references, and the validation manifest\n46\t- A tutorial packaged per the format can be run through the validation harness against a target release, producing a deterministic pass/fail result\n47\t- The format supports both launch target types: workbench (notebook) tutorials and pipeline tutorials\n48\t- A tutorial's version and validation status can change without requiring a Dashboard release (packaging is independent of Dashboard release cadence)\n49\t- The portion of the format specification covering the pipeline launch target type is reviewed and signed off by the RHOAI Pipelines team (the team whose tutorial content and tooling build against the format but do not co-own it), with the sign-off recorded on the specification\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- HLR-3 (P1, primary): tutorial packaging format defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases\n54\t- Enables HLR-1 and HLR-2: the gallery and all curated tutorials are built against this format\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-af63cdb71743c457","agent_id":"ad50c4934507a86db","session_id":"0ad94842-2610-4147-8d08-4293ba16f19d","uuid":"168a64cb-e115-4fd9-826c-a08258076699","timestamp":"2026-10-23T20:02:51.885Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-a81f7d96b9514d04","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019"}
